[38;5;202m◂[0m [2m{'function': 'staking_pool_specs::join_staked_sui_spec', 'complexity': 'low', 'summary': "Merges two StakedSui objects by consuming `other` and adding its principal balance to `self`. The `other` object's UID is deleted and its principal Balance<SUI> is joined into `self.principal`. Aborts if the two objects have mismatched staking metadata (different pool_id or stake_activation_epoch).", 'role': "User-facing entry point (exposed as `StakedSui.join()`) that allows a holder to consolidate two staking receipts from the same pool and same activation epoch into one. Directly reachable only through `staking_pool::join_staked_sui`; no protocol state is modified — only the caller's own object is mutated.", 'aborts': [{'condition': '!is_equal_staking_metadata(self, &other)', 'reason': 'The two StakedSui objects differ in pool_id or stake_activation_epoch (EIncompatibleStakedSui = 12). is_equal_staking_metadata checks both fields for equality.'}], 'requires': ['self.pool_id == other.pool_id', 'self.stake_activation_epoch == other.stake_activation_epoch', 'self.principal.value() > 0 (implicitly guaranteed by MIN_STAKING_THRESHOLD invariant at creation)', 'other.principal.value() > 0 (implicitly guaranteed by MIN_STAKING_THRESHOLD invariant at creation)'], 'ensures': ['self.pool_id == old(self.pool_id)  (unchanged)', 'self.stake_activation_epoch == old(self.stake_activation_epoch)  (unchanged)', 'self.principal.value() == old(self.principal.value()) + old(other.principal.value())', 'other is destroyed (its UID is deleted, no live object remains)', 'self.principal.value() >= MIN_STAKING_THRESHOLD  (conservation: both addends are >= threshold, sum is strictly larger)'], 'observations': ['Balance::join is total (no abort) for u64 addition; an overflow of principal would require the combined principal to exceed u64::MAX (~1.8e19 MIST ≈ 1.8e10 SUI), which is beyond the total SUI supply, so this path is practically unreachable. The prover may need an assume or a bound to close this automatically.', 'The minimum-stake invariant is preserved post-join: since both inputs satisfy principal >= MIN_STAKING_THRESHOLD, the result satisfies it trivially. No split-like check is needed here, unlike in staking_pool::split.', 'No StakingPool state is touched; pending_stake, pool_token_balance, and exchange_rates are all unaffected. The join is purely a client-side object merge with no accounting impact until a future withdraw is requested.']}[0m

